  (B) THE COMPANION STATEMENT.  The same expansion makes the effective Poisson operator anisotropic,
      nu_e (delta_ij + L_e n_i n_j), so the phantom halo is squeezed along the external field with
      axis ratio sqrt(1 + L_e).  Deep external field: sqrt(1/2) = 0.7071.  This is what item 83 would test.
      g_ext =   0.01 a_0  ->  L_e = -0.4754,  phantom axis ratio = 0.7243
      g_ext =   0.10 a_0  ->  L_e = -0.4251,  phantom axis ratio = 0.7582
      g_ext =   1.00 a_0  ->  L_e = -0.2910,  phantom axis ratio = 0.8420
      g_ext =  10.00 a_0  ->  L_e = -0.0699,  phantom axis ratio = 0.9644

