  (C3) STRUCTURAL CONFOUNDS IN THE LOCAL GROUP TEST -- checked BEFORE the verdict is quoted (bug pattern 5).
       (i) M_dyn/M_b plotted against M_b shares its denominator with the abscissa, so ANY scatter in M_b
           induces a negative slope.  (ii) The dwarf's distance from its host sets g_ext (~D^-2) AND enters
           M_dyn ~ sigma^2 r_h ~ D and M_b ~ L ~ D^2, so M_dyn/M_b ~ 1/D: a pure distance error produces
           d log(ratio)/d log g_ext = (-1)/(-2) = +0.500 with no physics in it at all.
       measured own-mass slope was -0.509; the induced-by-construction value for a ratio against its
       own denominator with the observed spread is at least -0.3 to -1.0 depending on the M_b error.
       measured g_ext slope was +0.695; the distance-induced artefact alone is +0.500.
       VERDICT ON (C2): both Local-Group shape tests are structurally confounded and CANNOT decide the law.
       Only the Coma test is clean on this axis -- there g_obs and g_bar are tabulated independently and the
       distance is the cluster's, common to every object, so neither confound operates.

       selection control: the 'EFE-dominated only' cut (g_int < g_ext) removes compact/massive dwarfs.
         cut=ON   N= 34  median resid +1.084 dex  own-mass slope -0.509  g_ext slope +0.695
         cut=OFF  N= 41  median resid +0.806 dex  own-mass slope -0.502  g_ext slope +0.958

  MUTATION: with nu = 1 (Newtonian) the law predicts M_dyn/M_b = 1 exactly for every system, everywhere.
  The Coma UDGs measure a median discrepancy of 24.5, so the Newtonian alternative is excluded outright;
  the question this candidate asks is whether the EFE theorem's SHAPE -- environment only, own mass irrelevant --
  is what the data show.

  THE UPSILON LEVER.  M_dyn/M_b scales as 1/Upsilon, so d log(ratio)/d log Upsilon = -1 exactly for the
  AMPLITUDE test.  The SHAPE tests above (slope in the system's own mass, slope in the external field) are
  Upsilon-INVARIANT if Upsilon is common to the sample: a global Upsilon shift moves every point vertically
  by the same amount and cannot change either slope.  Demonstrated:
    Upsilon_V =  1.0: N= 36  median residual +1.275 dex   own-mass slope -0.513
    Upsilon_V =  2.0: N= 34  median residual +1.084 dex   own-mass slope -0.509
    Upsilon_V =  4.0: N= 29  median residual +0.902 dex   own-mass slope -0.499


